--!strict
-- GL enumerants used by TinyGL.
--
-- Every value below is copied verbatim from TinyGL's include/GL/gl.h (which is
-- itself derived from Mesa), so code ported from C keeps working unchanged.
--
-- The table is returned frozen.  These are enumerants: nothing in the port, and
-- nothing a caller should be doing, assigns to one, and the table is handed out to
-- every module as well as to callers through TinyGL.Enum, so a stray write would
-- otherwise be shared by all of them and show up as a rendering bug somewhere else.
-- Frozen, it is a plain error at the place that made the mistake.  Only this table
-- is frozen; every value in it is a number, so there is nothing nested to protect.

return table.freeze({
	GL_AMBIENT = 0x1200,
	GL_AMBIENT_AND_DIFFUSE = 0x1602,
